  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 237 PM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nThe pattern doesn't change appreciably late this week with the \ncenter of the ridge over the Tennessee Valley, trough over the \nwestern US, and Iowa on the periphery of the shortwave track. \nThis will keep the warmest conditions over southern Iowa with \nstorm chances highest late at night diminishing in the morning \nhours over northern Iowa. Into next weekend, there is a signal \nthe ridge axis amplifies over the Plains, which pushes storm \nchances north away from the state.",
